5X3f0fxO4YnVKVZP8p6hg"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5231785/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5231785","image":"https://i.discogs.com/clhERctjV1QemA1a1BA0KqoED5Uu7h0rnUULtXSsxFk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUyMzE3/ODUtMTU3MTE1MDkw/Ny01NTgyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/h4EHjP3vjb6e3vqu-BeBMWa2I1JZ1caN-3tqVvGgn6c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUyMzE3/ODUtMTU3MTE1MDkw/Ny01NTgyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"In 2005 [a=Gareth Jones] was hired to mix an album by [a=Men, Women & Children], a group that [a=Nick Hook (3)] was playing keyboards in at the time. Connecting over a shared love of synths and the simple fact that they were the only two non-musicians in the room, Jones and Hook struck up a friendship. Nearly a decade after their first meeting, the two finally decided to get in the studio together, in late 2014. Guided by a simple premise—no judgement—and a whole lot of psychedelic adventuring, the pair went to work, letting their unconscious lead the way as they pieced together a complex suite of field recordings and modular synth transmissions.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5231785","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":2719,"name":"Gareth Jones"},{"active":true,"id":1507104,"name":"Nick Conceller"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5231785-Spiritual-Friendship","type":"artist","urls":["http://spiritualfriendship.site/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5929138/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5929138","image":"https://i.discogs.com/wrvqK_AJrqhbas7nvakd37IODY8rg1ILst32VyZfcLc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:402/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU5Mjkx/MzgtMTU3ODIyNTM2/Mi0yNzY2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/LNsSNs9JAZ0QB0A3qnJlXCyR4SZ8eJ6FBBzP3feRRHY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU5Mjkx/MzgtMTU3ODIyNTM2/Mi0yNzY2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Musician based in Melbourne, Australia.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5929138","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5929138-Escape-Artist-2","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/escapeartistaus","https://www.facebook.com/escapeartistaus/","https://www.residentadvisor.net/dj/escapeartist"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6059405/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6059405","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:6059405","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["A. Kisnorbo"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/6059405-Amy-Kisnorbo","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/75187/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"75187","image":"https://i.discogs.com/B2mCgzAi4YQF5WXgd5LCXETHsznrwaNoKlfbKGdP0B8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:409/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc1MTg3/LTE1MzE2NDk3OTMt/NDk1NC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Ccz8zPTbbrGQ62kAxkoC4PQjF_davWY_C-sVsb1T8uE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc1MTg3/LTE1MzE2NDk3OTMt/NDk1NC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American Miami Bass group from Miami which had its greatest commercial success from the late 1980s to the early 1990s. They were founded in Riverside, Ca. by the original line-up of Fresh Kid Ice, DJ Mr. Mixx and Amazing Vee; the latter of which left the group shortly after production of their first single, \"Revelation\". The group's most well-known line up was composed of Luke Campbell, Fresh Kid Ice, Mr. Mixx, and Brother Marquis. They were considerably controversial in the U.S. due to the sexually explicit content in their songs, particularly on their 1989 album As Nasty as They Wanna Be.\r\n\r\n[a=The New 2 Live Crew] was a small follow-up group - please don't use an ANV for The 2 Live Crew.\r\nThe Krew is also another artist.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:75187","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":257044,"name":"The Skyywalker All Stars"}],"members":[{"active":true,"id":93043,"name":"Luther Campbell"},{"active":true,"id":174211,"name":"David Hobbs"},{"active":true,"id":401058,"name":"Mark Ross"},{"active":true,"id":401059,"name":"Chris Wong Won"},{"active":false,"id":8153528,"name":"Yuri Vielot"}],"namevariations":["2","2 Live","2 Live CRew","2 Live Crew","2 Live Croew","2 Live Cru","2 Live Rock","2-Live Crew","2LC","2Live Crew","Live Crew","Live Crew 2","Original 2 Live Crue","The 2 Life Crew","The 2Live Crew","The Two Live Crew","Two Live Crew","Z Live Crew","快活幫"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/75187-The-2-Live-Crew","type":"artist","urls":["http://the2livecrew.com/","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2_Live_Crew","http://www.xyno.de/index.html","https://www.youtube.com/@TheReal2LiveCrew/featured"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/78/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"78","image":"https://i.discogs.com/XAMR1UBEtcU4s6tEuweZVJR0Yp4VfdtyzH5hBZPRfVc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:480/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc4LTE3/MzU2MjY4MTktNDE4/Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/uB6gt7yR9NZM2Q9NLMLDy4jT2m2Rd-KF85hrZZTUR2Y/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc4LTE3/MzU2MjY4MTktNDE4/Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Brazilian fusion jazz trio founded by Bertrami (keyboards), Conti (percussion) & Malheiros (bass). The 3 had been playing in the bossa nova and jazz scene of Rio as live and session musicians, and were living in the same bohemian block in Copacabana when Bertrami invited the two others to join him. They first recorded together as a trio the late 1960s as Projeto III, then recorded an album of covers as Som Ambiente in 1972. (That same year also saw a 7\" EP as [a14806835], a quartet fronted by singer Fabiola.) In 1973 they changed the band's name to Azymuth, inspired by a Marcos & Paulo Sérgio Valle song. (They also backed Marcos Valle on his [url=https://www.discogs.com/master/167268-Marcos-Valle-Previs%C3%A3o-Do-Tempo]Previsão Do Tempo[/url] album released in 1973.) In 1975 they released their first album, initially titled Azimüth. It featured the hit Linha Do Horizonte. In 1976 they scored another minor hit with Melô Da Cuíca. In 1979 Jazz Carnival became another hit, and 1980's Dear Limmertz also became a popular staple. The trio moved to the United States in the early 1980s, producing a number of albums that never came out in Brazil, and placing their bets on a mix of samba, funk and jazz that they defined as MPB-jazz (referring to Música Popular Brasileira). The main composer, keyboardist [a550629] left the group in 1988, and was replaced by Jota Moraes and by Marinho Boffa, but Bertrami returned in the middle of the following decade, when the group signed with the label Far Out. After Bertrami died in 2012, keyboardist Kiko Continentino joined drummer Ivan \"Mamão\" Conti and bassist Alex Malheiros in 2015 to continue the band. After the death of [a300989] in April 2023, [a3985129] joined as Conti's successor.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:78","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":730178,"name":"Hot Stuff Band"},{"id":934487,"name":"Som Ambiente"},{"id":2972135,"name":"Projeto III"},{"id":4294513,"name":"Apolo IV"},{"id":4305200,"name":"Alan And His Orchestra"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":300988,"name":"Alex Malheiros"},{"active":true,"id":300989,"name":"Ivan Conti"},{"active":true,"id":400242,"name":"Fernando Moraes"},{"active":false,"id":471678,"name":"Jota Moraes"},{"active":false,"id":550629,"name":"José Roberto Bertrami"},{"active":true,"id":658353,"name":"Marinho Boffa"},{"active":true,"id":1215821,"name":"Kiko Continentino"},{"active":true,"id":3985129,"name":"Renato \"Massa\" Calmon"}],"namevariations":["Azimuth","Azimüth","Azy Muth","Azymuth - Azymuth","Azymüth","Bertrami E Conjunto Azimuth","Conj. Azimuth","Conjunto Azimute","Conjunto Azimuth","Zé Roberto E Conjunto Azimuth","アジムス"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/78-Azymuth","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.azymuth.rio/","https://azymuth.bandcamp.com/","https://marcosvalleazymuth.bandcamp.com/","https://www.facebook.com/azymuthoficial","https://www.instagram.com/azymuthoficial/","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm14563860/","https://linktr.ee/azymuth","https://myspace.com/azymuth","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azymuth","https://www.youtube.com/@azymuthoficial","https://www.faroutrecordings.com/collections/azymuth","https://www.jazzisdead.com/azymuth"]}},"/api/discogs/label/117386/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"117386","image":"https://i.discogs.com/ilZSMSlekBV8QsQLei8bf3Z5qYocJwBopUsKLgrxYYs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTExNzM4/Ni0xNTkyNjY3NTgw/LTgxNDIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/zysRUP6loIHvvPFtB-mOtQA2qS7xNRvu47v4ovczPa8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTExNzM4/Ni0xNTkyNjY3NTgw/LTgxNDIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Electronic and dance music label from Washington DC","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:117386","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":[{"id":1587116,"name":"YES MIX"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/117386-Future-Times","type":"label","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/pages/FUTURE-TIMES/252230770072","https://futuretimes.bandcamp.com/","http://www.futuretimes.org/","https://soundcloud.com/future-times"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1708137/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1708137","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1708137","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1708137-Keck","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/2552458/profile":{"cached":true,